quran[27]{c,v,t}:
  68,16,"Soon, We shall brand him on (his) trunk-like nose."
  68,17,"Indeed, We have tested them (i.e. the inhabitants of Mecca) as We tested the owners of a (particular) garden (in Yemen) when they swore they would harvest (all) its fruit in the early morning."
  68,18,They did not make any exception (for Allah’s will or by setting aside a portion for the poor).
  68,19,"Then, your Lord’s visitation (of a disaster) struck that (garden) while they were asleep."
  68,20,"So, that (garden) became like a harvested field."
  68,21,"At dawn, they called out to one another:"
  68,22,‘Leave early to your field if you want to pick the fruits.’
  68,23,So they set off whispering to one another:
  68,24,‘Do not let any poor person enter your garden today.’
  68,25,"So they proceeded early in the morning, (considering themselves) competent to execute their plan."
  68,26,"When they saw it (ruined), they said: ‘We must have lost our way."
  68,27,No! We have indeed been deprived (of our livelihood).’
  68,28,The most sensible of them said: ‘Did I not tell you: ‘Why do you not glorify (Allah)?’’
  68,29,(Then) they said: ‘Glory be to our Lord! We have surely been wrongdoers!’
  68,30,"Then they turned to one another, blaming each other."
  68,31,"They said: ‘Woe to us! Indeed, we have been rebellious."
  68,32,Perhaps our Lord will give us a better one in its place. We are indeed turning to our Lord with hope.’
  68,33,Such is the punishment (of this world). But the punishment of the Hereafter is far greater if only they knew.
  68,34,"Indeed, for the God-conscious, the Gardens of Bliss will be with their Lord."
  68,35,Shall We then treat the submitters like the guilty?
  68,36,What is the matter with you? How do you judge?
  68,37,Do you have a scripture in which you read:
  68,38,that you shall have in it (i.e. the next world) whatever you choose?
  68,39,Or do you have any pledges binding on Us until the Day of Resurrection that you shall have whatever you decide (for yourselves)?
  68,40,"Ask them (O Prophet), which of them shall guarantee that (baseless assertion)!"
  68,41,"Or do they have any partners (supporting this assertion)? Then, let them produce their partners if they are truthful."
  68,42,"The Day when the Catastrophic Occurrence (of the Last Hour) is disclosed, they (i.e. the guilty) will be summoned to prostrate, but they will not be able to do so."
